<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρύγιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>Harm.</u>
			1
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φρύξ</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Phrygian,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ αἴας . . Φρυγίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					548
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείματα Φ.</span>
			the terrors <i>of the Phrygian goddess,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				457
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. νόμοι, μέλεα,</span>
			<u>Phrygian</u> music, esp. of music played on the flute,
			said to have been invented by Marsyas, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1426
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				545
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. αὐλοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					127
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶσα βακχεία . . μάλιστα . . ἐστὶν ἐν
					τοῖς αὐλοῖς . . : ὁ διθύραμβος ὁμολογουμένως δοκεῖ
					εἶναι Φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1342b7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Φρυγίον [ἁρμονίας] τὸ ἔνθεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. διὰ πασῶν εἶδος, τόνος,
				τρόπος,</span>
			<u>Phrygian</u> scale, <i><span class="en">
				Cleonid.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				9
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alyp.
				<u>Diat.</u>
				7
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. λίθος,</span> an <i>aluminous</i>
			kind of <i>pumice-stone,</i> used by dyers, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.123
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
